  "verdict_2026_09_28": "The previous verdict here read 'SUPPORTED'. Withdrawn. All three quantities tested are identities that hold whether or not GRH is true: |G(chi)| = sqrt(q) and |epsilon(chi)| = 1 are Gauss-sum facts about characters, and g_chi = 1 holds on the whole critical line, so it returns 1 at a non-zero of L(s,chi) exactly as at a zero. A check that cannot fail is not support. What survives: on the critical strip of L, |g_chi| = 1 forces Re(s) = 1/2 - a re-encoding of GRH, not evidence for it. See docs/PREDICTION_LEDGER.md PL-22 and experiments/chi_rho_vacuity_0_over_0.py.",
